== Bits Available ==
Booster Cookies allow players to generate {{bits}}, each Cookie has a limit to how many {{bits}} can be generated, which changes with [[Fame Ranks]] and [[Museum/Milestones|Museum Milestones]]. Bits are generated every half an hour by {{green|5.20833%}} (precisely {{green|1/19.2}}) of what one Cookie can provide, which can be increased by {{Item|Bits Talisman}}. Additionally, {{bits}} are awarded from defeating Bosses, finishing dungeons or participating in Events across Skyblock. (See [[Bits#Earning|Earning Bits]] for more details)
{{:Fame Ranks/Table}}

== Trivia ==<!--
* {{Red|WARNING}}: Currently, there is an extremely rare bug that the Booster Cookie boost can randomly bug out and will be removed when moving between servers in SkyBlock. This is not visual or temporary; the only way to get back the cookie boost is through consuming another cookie.
*There is an option to buy more cookies at once from [[Elizabeth]]; however, buying more will not grant the player any extras or a discount compared to simply buying one cookie at a time.-->
* There is a purchase limit of 192 '''Booster Cookies''' per day.
* Disabling a [[Potion]] effect does not pause it; instead, it simply stops the effect from working on the player. Any duration timers will still tick down as normal, even when disabled.
* As part of compensation for the Hypixel Maintenance that occurred from 17 June 2021 to 22 June 2021, players who had a {{Pink|Cookie Buff}} active when the maintenance took place were compensated with an untradeable '''Booster Cookie''' via {{NPCSprite|Jerry}}.
** These cookies, like the free cookie given to a player by {{NPCSprite|Elizabeth}}, cannot be sold to the [[Bazaar]], [[Auction House]] or to [[NPC]]s and cannot be dropped.
* Attempting to drop a non-normal cookie on the ground will tell the player {{RawMctxt|&6You may not drop this Booster Cookie!}}.<!--
*{{Code|/auction}}/{{Code|/ah}} cannot be used while in a dungeon.-->
*If the player was in a [[Co-op]] with player(s) who have not claimed the free cookie, they were able to get two or more free cookies by placing the free cookie(s) in a chest on their {{Zone|Private Island}}.
**This doesn't work anymore. The free Cookies are now tied to specific players. When another tries to consume it, the game sends this message: {{RawMctxt|&cThis cookie was given to another player! You may not consume it!}}
*A player can still obtain a '''Booster Cookie''' on [[Bingo]] through the Security Quest. However, because the player cannot spend Bits at {{NPCSprite|Elizabeth}} on this profile, the only way they can be spent is through tuning templates with {{NPCSprite|Maxwell}}, or refreshing [[Experiments|Experiments]].
**This allows for the usual bonuses of a Booster Cookie, such as Wisdom, Magic Find, and flight.

